  "chapter": {
    "number": 17,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          "I perish, carried away by the wind, and I seek for burial, and obtain it not."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          "Weary I entreat; and what have I done? and strangers have stolen my goods."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          "Who is this? let him join hands with me."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          "For you have hid their heart from wisdom; therefore you shall not exalt them."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          "He shall promise mischief to his companions: but their eyes have failed for their children."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          "But you have made me a byword among the nations, and I am become a scorn to them."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          "For my eyes are dimmed through pain; I have been grievously beset by all."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          "Wonder has seized true men upon this; and let the just rise up against the transgressor."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          "But let the faithful hold on his own way, and let him that is pure of hands take courage."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          "Howbeit, do you⌃ all strengthen yourselves and come now, for I do not find truth in you."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          "My days have passed in groaning, and my heart-strings are broken."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          "I have turned the night into day: the light is short because of darkness."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          "For if I remain, Hades is my habitation: and my bed has been made in darkness."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          "I have called upon death to be my father, and corruption to be my mother and sister."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          "Where then is yet my hope? or where shall I see my good?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          "Will they go down with me to Hades, or shall we go down together to the tomb?"
        ]
      }
    ],
